Why I want to teach here?

CMFI BHS has a reputation for shaping disciplined, well-rounded students who go on to succeed in science and technical fields. I want to teach here because I believe my engineering background can help bridge the gap between classroom theory and real-world application, giving students a reason to see physics, chemistry, and mathematics as tools for solving problems, not just subjects to memorize for exams. Teaching at CMFI BHS would let me contribute directly to strengthening STEM education in a school community I respect.
What I will bring?

I bring four years of hands-on teaching experience alongside a civil engineering education that reinforces the practical relevance of every concept I teach. My coursework in structural design, mechanics, and materials gives me concrete, real-life examples to draw from when explaining Newton's laws, chemical reactions, or algebraic relationships. I am also proficient in AutoCAD, Revit, and MATLAB, which I can use to make abstract concepts visual and easier for students to grasp. Beyond technical knowledge, I bring patience, adaptability, and a track record of helping students who struggle with these subjects build genuine confidence.
My teaching philosophy.

I believe every student can understand physics, chemistry, and mathematics when the material is connected to something they can see, touch, or reason through step by step. My philosophy is to teach from first principles: build understanding before memorization, encourage students to ask "why" as much as "how," and use real examples from engineering and daily life to make abstract ideas concrete. I also believe a classroom should be a safe place to make mistakes, since mistakes are often where the deepest learning happens.
I would welcome the opportunity to bring this experience and philosophy to CMFI BHS and would be glad to discuss my application further at your convenience.

Respectfully,

